{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraphView(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Subscripts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-2n5fj","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-34kf9","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-40a5z","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-7lnri","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-16yvl","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-3uhp3","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)-1tfjm","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)-8bx4q"],"generated":true,"title":"Subscripts"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/GraphAdaptor-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L31","fileName":"SubgraphView.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SubgraphView","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The kept vertices appear in the base’s order at view indices ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":". The view keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"renumbered with one array load per entry. A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex at its base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are and, if an edge set was given, when it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices, an edge’s index being its rank","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"count per 64-bit word, and a rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices, except one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that keeps every vertex, which keeps the base’s rows and edge indices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base, so mutating the original doesn’t show through. The base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must have vertex indices; construction traps when ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphAdaptor"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, of: vertex]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]"},{"type":"text","text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" forms throw. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"title":"Subgr